explanation:
{
    "explanation": "Q1 calculates the fraction of players whose second activity date is exactly one day after their first activity date, counting each player at most once. Q2 calculates the fraction of players who have at least one instance where their second recorded activity is exactly one day after their first recorded activity. The key difference is that Q1's denominator counts distinct players from the TEMP subquery (which includes all players with at least one activity), while Q2's denominator counts distinct players from the entire ACTIVITY table (which is the same set). However, Q1's numerator counts players only if their second activity date is exactly one day after their first, while Q2's numerator counts players if they have any second activity that's one day after the previous activity (which could be problematic if a player has multiple activities on consecutive days after their first). The divergence occurs when a player has multiple activities where the second activity is one day after the first, but also has other activities that don't meet this condition. Q1 counts such players only once in the numerator, while Q2 might count them multiple times or incorrectly due to the ROWN=2 filter not guaranteeing it's the actual second activity date relative to the first.",
